> API and interpretation

This grammar uses decimal tokens without exponent notation; complete conversion
and complete byte consumption are now checked. Unary signs bind as atoms, so-2^2
is4 here, unlike conventions where power binds before unary minus. Runtime
syntax errors, selected depth/work/history limits and nonfinite arithmetic
failures are distinct. The selected event count excludes the internals of
decimal conversion, exponentiation and whitespace scanning; it is not a
wall-time benchmark.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

